From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wayne <wayne@nuvoton.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:48:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] plat: nuvoton: override por from sram when usb boot

When the board boots in USB mode (e.g., via USB download tool / NuWriter),
BL2 is executed in SRAM with por & PWRON_BOOT_MSK == PWRON_BOOT_USB.
Read the uint32_t value at address 0x2803FFFC as the specified POR value
so that BL2 can proceed to load the next boot image according to the
host-specified target boot interface (SPI, NAND, SD/eMMC, etc.).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Wayne <wayne@nuvoton.com>
---
 plat/nuvoton/ma35d0/ma35d0_io_storage.c | 4 ++++
 plat/nuvoton/ma35d1/ma35d1_io_storage.c | 4 ++++
 plat/nuvoton/ma35h0/ma35h0_io_storage.c | 4 ++++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/nuvoton/ma35d0/ma35d0_io_storage.c b/plat/nuvoton/ma35d0/ma35d0_io_storage.c
index a8b51c8..fbc3f6d 100755
--- a/plat/nuvoton/ma35d0/ma35d0_io_storage.c
+++ b/plat/nuvoton/ma35d0/ma35d0_io_storage.c
@@ -308,6 +308,10 @@ void ma35d0_io_setup(void)
 		por = mmio_read_32(SYS_PWRONPIN);
 		por = por << 8;
 	}
+	if ((por & PWRON_BOOT_MSK) == PWRON_BOOT_USB) {
+		printf("Boot from USB, will read SRAM-tail\n");
+		por = mmio_read_32(0x2803FFFC);
+	}
 	printf("POR: 0x%x\n", por);
 
 	switch (por & PWRON_BOOT_MSK) {
